cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "A receipt you cannot reproduce is an opinion. Cite the version that produced the one you kept."
title: "ingest-conservation-guard: receipts of bucket conservation for data ingestion"
abstract: >-
  Schema validation tells you whether one row is well formed; nothing tells you whether the
  set survived the transform. This package emits receipts of bucket conservation for data
  ingestion, migrations and catalogue sync, holding the identity
  dominio == imagen + rechazos + sin_clave + colisiones. Every bucket is counted by its own
  pass over the input and never derived from the others, because a derived bucket closes in
  the integers even when the counts are incompatible (68 + 0 + (-1) = 67). Exit codes are a
  contract: 0 conserved, 1 merged, 4 broken, and a guard that only ever returns success is
  indistinguishable from no guard. Zero dependencies, standard library only; receipts are
  deterministic and replayable without the wheel.
authors:
